<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Anglo-Mysore War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1780">1780</a>–<a href="/years/1784">1784</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> War (1780–1784) began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyder-ali">Hyder Ali</a> invaded the Carnatic and destroyed a British detachment at Pollilur in 1780. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eyre-coote">Eyre Coote</a> checked him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> Novo in 1781, and after Hyder's death in 1782 his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a>, aided for a time by the French, carried on the fight. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-mangalore">Treaty of Mangalore</a> of 1784 ended it on the basis of mutual <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/repatriation-of-cultural-property">restitution</a> of conquests.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-anglo-mysore-war.jpg" alt="Second Anglo-Mysore War" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Second_Anglo-Mysore_War_Horizontal_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
